## 3. How It Operates Under ONE Single Domain

Once deployed, Vercel gives you **one URL** (for example `https://greathire-teamora.vercel.app`):
- **Frontend SPA**: `https://greathire-teamora.vercel.app/`
- **Backend Health Check**: `https://greathire-teamora.vercel.app/api/health`
- **All API routes**: `https://greathire-teamora.vercel.app/api/...`

If you have a **Custom Domain** (e.g. `teamora.greathire.com` or `greathire.com`):
1. In your Vercel project, go to **Settings** > **Domains**.
2. Add your domain.
3. Add the DNS CNAME/A record provided by Vercel in your DNS registrar.
4. Your entire app (Frontend + Backend) is live on your custom domain!

