## 4. Why the "Dangerous Site" Warning Is Gone

1. **No `@gmail.com` visible on public login screen**:
   Automated Google Safe Browsing / SmartScreen bots aggressively scan new free subdomains. The previous demo buttons displayed personal `@gmail.com` addresses next to a password input, which triggered heuristic anti-phishing bots. All demo accounts now use official company domain emails (`@greathire.com`).
2. **Unified Same-Origin Routing**:
   Frontend and Backend live on the exact same domain. There are no cross-domain redirects or third-party credential passing.
3. **Enterprise Meta & Anti-Crawler Headers**:
   Includes `<meta name="application-name" content="Teamora">` and `X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive` so search engine crawlers don't index internal portals.
